WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.600
What if nobody tells you the current?

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.875
Then you measure it yourself, with two fixes.

3
00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:08.000
Follow it on screen.

4
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.625
You have a good fix at eight hundred.

5
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:15.250
You run your course and speed, and plot where you should be at ten hundred.

6
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.000
That’s your dead reckoning position.

7
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.600
At ten hundred you take another fix, and it isn’t on the DR.

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.625
It lies three miles away, bearing one five zero true from the DR.

9
00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:29.675
So what pushed you there?

10
00:00:29.925 --> 00:00:31.375
The current.

11
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:36.600
Its set is the direction from the DR to the fix: one five zero true.

12
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:40.325
Its drift is the distance divided by the time.

13
00:00:40.575 --> 00:00:42.775
Three miles in two hours.

14
00:00:43.775 --> 00:00:45.575
One and a half knots.

15
00:00:45.825 --> 00:00:48.700
Now use it, to correct your next course.

16
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:53.675
And remember the direction: from where you thought you were, to where you really are.

17
00:00:53.925 --> 00:00:55.725
That’s lesson eight.

18
00:00:55.975 --> 00:00:58.500
Current is named for where it goes.

19
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.100
Wind against current is trouble.

20
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.050
And set runs from DR to fix.

21
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.500
Next time: the compass.
